# Regression fixture for #98: a Float value reaching a bitwise op used
# to crash the compiled runtime helper outright ("expected an integer"),
# regardless of the target program -- as_bits/as_int (rust-runtime/src/
# ir/codegen.rs and ops.rs) never accepted Value::Float, a distinct
# fast-path variant separate from Value::Number. Checked here via the
# NATIVE `--patc` backend specifically, since that's the code path
# codegen.rs's as_bits fix (commit 1d88746) directly governs -- the
# equivalent case under --x64 hits a different, still-open bug (#102,
# a wrong NUMBER rather than a crash) and is intentionally not tested
# here to avoid conflating the two.
make a function called bandtest takes f returns done
  print(f band 255)
end
bandtest(1)
bandtest(1.0 + 61.0)
